## Candidate, preview, release

A candidate is the built version you intend to publish. A preview lets you inspect it. A release makes a verified version active. Treat these as separate states rather than three names for one button.

## Verify before promotion

Check the application route, required configuration, data connections and the main user task. Save the release identifier that passed those checks.

```bash
miosa app preview ./app --json
miosa app verify <release-id> ./app --json
miosa app promote <release-id> ./app --yes --json
```

## Recover the right thing

A failed operation may be recoverable without rebuilding. A broken active release may require a rollback. Inspect the current operation and release states before choosing either action.

## Practice the order

The [Shipping lab](/docs/learn/labs/shipping) makes the sequence explicit. It records local practice completion after you put the steps in the right order.
